{"id": "valpaca0001", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, you know, it's a very interesting story. I mean, there are so many different stories about how states got their names. Some of them were named after the king or queen at the time. Some of them were named after famous people from England. But then some of them were actually named after Native Americans, which is pretty cool. For example, Florida was named after the Spanish word for flowers because they thought that' s what they saw when they first came here. And New York was named after Duke of York, who later became King James II. So those are just a couple examples.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
