{"id": "valpaca0009", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Cubdari is a traditional Georgian dish made with flatbread, cheese, and herbs. To make it, you'll need to start by preparing the dough using flour, water, yeast, and salt. Kne ad the dough until it's smooth, then let it rise for about an hour. After that, roll out the dough into thin sheet s. Next, spread some melted cheese over the dough, followed by chopped fresh herbs like mint or parsley. Roll up the dough into a cylindrical shape and slice it into bite-sized pieces. You can serve cub dari as an appetizer or snack, often accompanied by a Georgian wine called qvevri wine. It' s a simple yet delicious way to enjoy the flavors of Georgia.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 36, "carrier_ended": null}
