{"id": "valpaca0037", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It's actually caused by plate tectonics. The Earth' s surface is broken up into several plates that float on the mantle below, and they move around very slowly. And when two of them colli de, they can form a vol cano if one of them goes under the other. That' s called subduction, and it causes a lot of the world' s volcanoes to form.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0041", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, there are a few ways to reduce your phone usage. First of all, you can try setting limits on how much time you spend on your phone each day. Many phones have built-in tools that let you set these limits. You can also turn off notifications for apps that distract you or don't really need constant updates. Another idea is to schedule specific times during the day when you check your phone, instead of checking it constantly throughout the day. Also, consider replacing some phone-based activities with other things, like reading a book or going for a walk.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
